## JavaScript Variables
-> Variables are used to store data.

## Variable Declaration
1. Using var
var name = "Sudarshan";

2. Using let
let age = 21;

3. Using const
const country = "India";


## Difference Between var, let and const
Keyword	        Value Change	    Scope
var	              Yes	        Function Scope
let	              Yes	        Block Scope
const	          No	        Block Scope


## Data Types in JavaScript

JavaScript has primitive data types.

1. Undefined
A variable declared but not assigned a value.

let x;
console.log(x);
Output
undefined

2. Null

Represents intentional absence of value.

let data = null;
console.log(data);
Output
null
JavaScript Oddity
typeof null
Output
object

Even though null means no value, JavaScript treats it as an object.
This is considered a historical bug in JavaScript.

3. Boolean

Stores true or false values.

let isLoggedIn = true;
4. Number

Stores numeric values.

let marks = 95;
5. String

Stores text values.

let course = "JavaScript";
6. Symbol

Used to create unique identifiers.

let id = Symbol("id");
JavaScript Syntax

Syntax is the set of rules for writing correct JavaScript programs.

Example
let name = "JavaScript";
console.log(name);
Syntax Rules
Statements usually end with semicolon ;
JavaScript is case-sensitive
Variables must follow naming rules


